{t: Use Me}
{st: Bill Withers}
{key: Em}
{tempo: 78}

{sot: Intro}
| Em7   A7    | Em7   A7    | Em7   A7    | Em7   A7    |
{eot}

{sot: Verse}
| Em7   A7    | Em7   A7    | Em7   A7    | Em7   A7    |
| Em7   A7    | Em7   A7    | Em7   A7    | Em7   A7    |
{eot}

{sot: Chorus}
| B7          | C7          | Em7   A7    | Em7   A7    |
{eot}

{sov: Notes}
Main Groove: The core driver is a syncopated two-bar funk vamp in E Dorian,
switching rapidly between Em7 and A7 (often played with an E minor clavinet
riff overlay).

Clavinet Riff: Focus heavily on the rhythmic pocket. The guitar supports the
keyboard pattern with tight, staccato 16th-note chucks and muted string scrapes.

Chorus Turnaround: The tension builds on the chromatic dominant step-up from
B7 to C7 before dropping back into the main Em7 to A7 groove.
{eov}